{"name":"Bronze Yellow","hex":"#737000","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bronze yellow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish brown colour, like that of bronze."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a yellowish brown colour, like that of bronze."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bronze_yellow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bronze","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is an alloy consisting primarily of copper, commonly with about 12–12.5% tin and often with the addition of other metals and sometimes non-metals or metalloids. These additions produce a range of alloys some of which are harder than copper alone or have other useful properties, such as strength, ductility, or machinability."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5e/Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg/330px-Bull%27s_head_ornament_for_a_lyre_MET_DP260070.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze","wikidata":"Q34095"},{"title":"Yellow","blocks":[{"text":"Yellow is a color between green and orange on the spectrum of light. It is evoked by light with a dominant wavelength of roughly 575–585 nm. It is a primary color in subtractive color systems, used in painting or color printing. In the RGB color model, used to create colors on television and computer screens, yellow is a secondary color made by combining red and green at equal intensity. Carotenoids give the characteristic yellow color to autumn leaves, corn, canaries, daffodils, and lemons, as well as egg yolks, buttercups, and bananas. They absorb light energy and protect plants from photo damage in some cases. Sunlight has a slight yellowish hue when the Sun is near the horizon, due to atmospheric scattering of shorter wavelengths."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg/330px-Cornwall_Daffodils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yellow","wikidata":"Q943"},{"title":"Bronze (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Bronze is a metallic brown color which resembles the metal alloy bronze. An archaic term for it was aeneous."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png/330px-Bronze_medal_for_bravery_%28Austria-Hungary%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bronze_(color)","wikidata":"Q2778382"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-1280px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif/lossy-page1-500px-Egypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of_Art.tif.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEgypt%2C_Greco-Roman_Period%2C_probably_Ptolemaic_Dynasty_-_Statuette_of_Isis_and_Horus_-_1940.613_-_Cleveland_Museum_of